diff --git a/doc/dev/rocksdb-submission-counters.rst b/doc/dev/rocksdb-submission-counters.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..cbce7bf57f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/dev/rocksdb-submission-counters.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+RocksDB submission counters for snapshot experiments
+===================================================
+
+The ``snapWrite`` branch starts at Ceph 17.2.7 commit
+``b12291d110049b2f35e32e0de30d70e9a4c060d2``. It adds three counters to
+``RocksDBStore::submit_common()``, shared by the synchronous and asynchronous
+KeyValueDB submission APIs:
+
+* ``rocksdb.submitted_txns``: successfully submitted WriteBatches, including
+  empty batches used for synchronization.
+* ``rocksdb.submitted_ops``: the sum of ``WriteBatch::Count()``. Repeated
+  updates to the same key are counted separately. Put, Delete, SingleDelete,
+  DeleteRange and Merge records contribute according to RocksDB's batch count.
+* ``rocksdb.submitted_bytes``: the sum of ``WriteBatch::GetDataSize()`` captured
+  before ``DB::Write()``. This includes encoded keys, values, operation tags,
+  length fields, column-family identifiers and the batch header. An empty
+  batch currently contributes its 12-byte header and zero updates.
+
+Only successful calls are counted. Failed submissions contribute zero. Each
+successful resubmission of the same transaction is counted again. Measurements
+use cumulative input, not unique keys or net database growth. Reads and
+RocksDB-internal WAL, flush and compaction writes do not increment these
+counters. There are three counter updates per successful submission; no
+per-record traversal or logging is added to the hot path.
+
+Scope and limitations
+---------------------
+
+An OSD's database is shared by its pools, so these counters cover all
+submissions to that OSD's RocksDBStore. They do not attribute bytes to pools.
+Run the baseline and snapshot workloads sequentially and collect deltas on
+all participating OSDs. MONs and other programs linked with this implementation
+also expose these counters if rebuilt, but their values are outside the OSD
+measurement.
+
+These are serialized input bytes at the KeyValueDB/RocksDB boundary, not SSD
+writes, unencoded application metadata, or database space usage. BlueStore
+deferred transactions can contain user data as well as metadata. Check
+``bluestore.issued_deferred_write_bytes`` during the experiment; any increase
+must be investigated or reported separately before interpreting the input as
+pure metadata. These three counters do not filter deferred records.
+
+The counters are process-local and start over after a process restart or
+``perf reset rocksdb``. Their three fields are updated separately, so take
+final measurements after the workload has drained. They are available without
+enabling ``rocksdb_perf`` or verbose debug logging.
+
+Reading and resetting
+---------------------
+
+For example, using the lab's matching client wrapper on node4::
+
+  /home/cyf/ceph-lab-17.2.7/ceph.sh tell osd.0 perf dump -f json \
+    | jq '.rocksdb | {submitted_txns, submitted_ops, submitted_bytes}'
+
+The existing reset command resets the entire RocksDB counter group, including
+its latency and compaction counters::
+
+  /home/cyf/ceph-lab-17.2.7/ceph.sh tell osd.0 perf reset rocksdb
+
+For serial experiments, recording a baseline and subtracting it preserves the
+original counter history. If resetting, drain the preceding workload first,
+reset all measured OSDs, then take a new baseline to account for background
+submissions. Neither reset nor reading a counter clears the database or cache.
+
+For a workload writing ``W`` client bytes, sum the OSD deltas to obtain ``L``.
+Compare ``L_snap`` and ``L_base`` for identical logical workloads. Report the
+snapshot increment as ``(L_snap - L_base) / W`` and the extra bytes per object
+as ``(L_snap - L_base) / object_count``. Keep pool creation, initial data loading,
+snapshot creation (unless explicitly measured), deletion and snaptrim outside
+the overwrite measurement windows.
+
+Validation
+----------
+
+Build ``ceph-osd`` and ``ceph_test_keyvaluedb``. Run the submission-counter
+tests in a disposable working directory; the test fixture creates and removes
+``kv_test_temp_dir`` relative to that directory::
+
+  ceph_test_keyvaluedb --gtest_filter='KeyValueDB/KVTest.SubmittedCounters*/0'
+
+The tests cover synchronous and asynchronous submission, repeated updates,
+deletes, merges, reads, compaction, empty synchronization batches, counter
+reset and failed writes to a read-only database.
diff --git a/src/kv/RocksDBStore.cc b/src/kv/RocksDBStore.cc
index de2a486ae5..4b5620a270 100644
--- a/src/kv/RocksDBStore.cc
+++ b/src/kv/RocksDBStore.cc
@@ -1251,6 +1251,13 @@ int RocksDBStore::do_open(ostream &out,
   plb.add_time_avg(l_rocksdb_write_delay_time, "rocksdb_write_delay_time", "Rocksdb write delay time");
   plb.add_time_avg(l_rocksdb_write_pre_and_post_process_time, 
       "rocksdb_write_pre_and_post_time", "total time spent on writing a record, excluding write process");
+  plb.add_u64_counter(l_rocksdb_submitted_txns, "submitted_txns",
+      "Successfully submitted WriteBatches, including empty batches");
+  plb.add_u64_counter(l_rocksdb_submitted_ops, "submitted_ops",
+      "Updates in successfully submitted WriteBatches");
+  plb.add_u64_counter(l_rocksdb_submitted_bytes, "submitted_bytes",
+      "Serialized bytes in successfully submitted WriteBatches, including headers",
+      nullptr, PerfCountersBuilder::PRIO_USEFUL, unit_t(UNIT_BYTES));
   logger = plb.create_perf_counters();
   cct->get_perfcounters_collection()->add(logger);
 
@@ -1552,12 +1559,20 @@ int RocksDBStore::submit_common(rocksdb::WriteOptions& woptions, KeyValueDB::Tra
   _t->bat.Iterate(&bat_txc);
   *_dout << " Rocksdb transaction: " << bat_txc.seen.str() << dendl;
   
+  // Measure the input before RocksDB adds its own WAL/SST/compaction writes.
+  // Both submit_transaction() and submit_transaction_sync() use this path.
+  const auto submitted_bytes = _t->bat.GetDataSize();
+  const auto submitted_ops = _t->bat.Count();
   rocksdb::Status s = db->Write(woptions, &_t->bat);
   if (!s.ok()) {
     RocksWBHandler rocks_txc(*this);
     _t->bat.Iterate(&rocks_txc);
     derr << __func__ << " error: " << s.ToString() << " code = " << s.code()
          << " Rocksdb transaction: " << rocks_txc.seen.str() << dendl;
+  } else {
+    logger->inc(l_rocksdb_submitted_txns);
+    logger->inc(l_rocksdb_submitted_ops, submitted_ops);
+    logger->inc(l_rocksdb_submitted_bytes, submitted_bytes);
   }
 
   if (cct->_conf->rocksdb_perf) {
